statement:
Let n, l be natural numbers, K0 >= 0, sigma > 0, E >= 0, f : R^n -> R^l 1-Lipschitz on closedBall 0 (sigma/2), and W : R^n -> R measurable. Put B1 := ball 0 (3 sigma/8) and |Df(x)|^2 := hsNormSq(fderiv R f x). Assume:
(H1') for a.e. x: if x is in B1, then W(x) = 0 or W(x) >= 1;
(H2) L^n(B1 cap {W = 0}) <= ofReal(K0 E sigma^n);
(H3) the lower Lebesgue integral over B1 of ofReal(|Df|^2 W) is <= ofReal(K0 E sigma^n).
Then x -> |Df(x)|^2 is integrable on B1, and int_{B1} |Df|^2 dL^n <= (1 + n) K0 E sigma^n.
